file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-223733-backend-dev-1--b08fae58/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":90,"content":"- MARATHON-2 fixed SQLite as SoT and Redis as ephemeral fan-out only. Storing tokens in Redis would break “any node accepts the same token” after Redis `SIGKILL` and contradicts MARATHON-14. Shared SQLite is the only persistence already wired on every node.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-222319-backend-dev-1--99c51c28/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":64,"content":"Create /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground and keeps the cluster serving while alive. Launch three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, :8002 and a local redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379. Self-contained (no remote services, no DinD). Respawning: if an HTTP node is SIGKILLed it must come back within 60s without external action; if Redis is SIGKILLed, start.sh must respawn it. Stub GET / on each node and GET /api/health returning 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports 8000/8001/8002. Choose language/framework and shared durable storage layout for the cluster.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":71,"content":"This task boots the Huddle cluster so the verifier (and every later feature task) has a live, self-contained process tree: `/app/start.sh` stays in the foreground, supervises a local Redis on `127.0.0.1:6379` and three identical HTTP nodes on `127.0.0.1:8000/8001/8002`, and respawns any of those children after `SIGKILL`. Each node exposes a stub `GET /` and the contracted `GET /api/health`. The design also locks language/framework and the shared durable storage layout that Auth, messages, fan-out, IRC, and the SPA will all assume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":82,"content":"| Process supervisor | **`/app/start.sh`** (bash): create dirs, ensure venv+deps, start Redis + 3 Uvicorn workers, foreground wait loop with respawn |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":89,"content":"- A shell supervisor matches the verifier contract (`./start.sh` foreground) and can respawn both HTTP and Redis without DinD or external orchestrators.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":96,"content":"| Redis as primary DB | Contradicts Redis-`SIGKILL` resilience (writes must succeed without Redis). |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-221719-app-architect-1--6d8c9266/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":67,"content":"Create /app/start.sh that stays in the foreground and keeps the cluster serving while alive. Launch three HTTP nodes on 127.0.0.1:8000, :8001, :8002 and a local redis-server on 127.0.0.1:6379. Self-contained (no remote services, no DinD). Respawning: if an HTTP node is SIGKILLed it must come back within 60s without external action; if Redis is SIGKILLed, start.sh must respawn it. Stub GET / on each node and GET /api/health returning 200 {status:ok, node_id} with node_id 0/1/2 matching ports 8000/8001/8002. Choose language/framework and shared durable storage layout for the cluster.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":15,"totalMatchedLines":15,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-be5f10cc-edd0-44a3-bb4b-28e8efbc226f-9\nfc_3a3f82ea-4591-9801-8230-9d9bec7bf706_2","startedAtMs":"1787438773199","completedAtMs":"1787438773530"},"model_call_id":"c64c3111-59ba-494a-830c-f5095298259d-2-8j7o","session_id":"6ee90dfc-ec75-48c4-8b56-cd9437a916e3","timestamp_ms":1787438773560}
